WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.420
- Welcome back y'all after nine seasons,

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.050
as a Real Housewife of Atlanta,

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.960
our next guest left the show last year

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.750
and promptly went on to
polish her first book.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:11.540
It's called the Pursuit of
Porsha and it's out now.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.746
Please welcome Porsha Williams.

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:16.329
(upbeat music)

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.400
You are like so beautiful.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.233
- Thank you.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:36.750
- Yes, and your dress is so
perfect for our color scheme.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:37.583
I love everything.

00:00:37.583 --> 00:00:39.060
- You know, I know your
show is very colorful,

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.980
very energetic. So I was
like, I'm going to pop.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.412
- Oh you did? Well done.

00:00:42.412 --> 00:00:43.245
(Porsha chuckling)
It's so good.

00:00:43.245 --> 00:00:44.078
It's so beautiful.

00:00:44.078 --> 00:00:45.340
And you, we both have young kids,

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:46.330
but you have a two-year-old, right?

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:47.163
- Yes.
- [Kelly] Two-year-old boy?

00:00:47.163 --> 00:00:49.020
- She's two. Girl.
- [Kelly] Oh she, girl, girl.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.900
- Yeah, Pilar she will
be three March 22nd.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:52.733
- [Kelly] Oh, okay.

00:00:52.733 --> 00:00:53.566
I'm in April. Okay.

00:00:53.566 --> 00:00:55.840
- Yeah. There she is.
- Wait, is that an Aries?

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.220
Is that an Aries? You got an Aries?

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:58.660
- I'm not into signs, so...

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.740
- I think she's an Aries,
she gon lead the world. Okay.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.160
- Oh, she's leading the house.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.000
- Then she's an Aries.
- So she's starting with us,

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:04.885
and then she's gon lead the world.

00:01:04.885 --> 00:01:06.760
(kelly chuckling)
That's how that work.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.490
- But you dedicated your book
to your daughter and wrote,

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:12.580
I love this, it says mommy's
tears will never be your fear.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.720
So what does that mean to you?

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:15.553
- A lot of different things

00:01:15.553 --> 00:01:16.810
that I've gone through in my life,

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.710
some were difficult.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:19.750
Some are great.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.260
I want her to learn from them.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:22.480
You know, I've already cried those tears.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.200
She doesn't have to go through that.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.033
So hopefully,

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:28.760
she will be the ending of some
of those generational curses

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:29.959
and things that I had gone through.

00:01:29.959 --> 00:01:31.829
- Break the cycle.
- Break the cycle.

00:01:31.829 --> 00:01:32.710
(applause)

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:33.870
And that's what the book is about.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.660
So hopefully when she
grows up and reads it,

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:36.676
that's what she'll get from it.

00:01:36.676 --> 00:01:39.490
- I love it. It's such a beautiful thing.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.460
You actually share your
fertility struggle,

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:42.350
which is a brave thing to do.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.588
I've had friends that
have struggled for years

00:01:43.588 --> 00:01:45.230
with fertility issues.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.570
- Yeah.
- And it's a hard thing to do

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:50.290
because people don't realize
how much women take that on.

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:51.790
Even though you have no control over it.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:52.990
And it's just your body,

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:54.390
they're like, what's wrong with me?

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.420
And that's a big thing to like
come out and be open with.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:57.760
But I thank you for it.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.610
Cause there's a lot of women
that will benefit from this.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:02.720
- And that's the thing, you know, people,

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.660
you think what your
body is supposed to do.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:05.890
So then when you get pregnant

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:08.300
and it's not as easy and
people don't talk about it,

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.760
you think you're alone.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.620
And for me as a black woman,

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:12.810
I suffered with fibroids

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:14.583
and we suffer with them the most.

00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:15.416
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:02:15.416 --> 00:02:16.249
- Highest percentage to have fibroids.

00:02:16.249 --> 00:02:17.450
- I have people in my
family with fibroids.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:18.283
- Yeah.

00:02:18.283 --> 00:02:19.116
- It's hurtful.

00:02:19.116 --> 00:02:20.280
It's painful.
- It really is.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.100
But the biggest thing is
that it went undiagnosed

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.310
because doctors just aren't gonna ask you

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:27.560
or just do an ultrasound
and look for fibroids.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:28.393
So for me,

00:02:28.393 --> 00:02:31.550
if I would have gotten my
fibroids diagnosed earlier on,

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.640
I probably wouldn't have
had to have the miscarriage

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:34.870
that I talk about in my book.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:35.703
- Ooh.

00:02:35.703 --> 00:02:39.460
- Because what happened was
the fibroids outgrew the fetus,

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:42.110
and then it resulted in the miscarriage.

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:44.990
- And it's just such a
hard thing to deal with.

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:46.570
Like watching friends
that have gone through it.

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:48.050
I can't imagine.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:49.130
I just think it's a,

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:50.380
it's a really beautiful thing.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.180
Cause I'm a very open person,

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:53.850
but there are things
that I don't talk about.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:54.683
And it's,

00:02:54.683 --> 00:02:55.770
it's amazing when people are strong enough

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.300
to talk about those things,

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.780
because it really does help sharing

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.730
and making it a topic of conversation.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:02.790
That it's a very normal thing
that happens unfortunately,

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:03.880
to a lot of people.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.650
- You know, when I went
through it, I felt so alone,

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:07.770
even though I was married
and my mom was right there,

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:11.310
you still feel like your body
has let you down in some way.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.540
And so that's why I joined
with March of Dimes.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:14.455
Hello, March of Dimes organization.

00:03:14.455 --> 00:03:15.820
- Oh I worked with March of Dimes.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:16.653
- You do?

00:03:16.653 --> 00:03:17.486
- Yeah. I've worked with March of,

00:03:17.486 --> 00:03:18.490
yeah.
- Yes, sister.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:21.040
- It's such a beautiful
organization to work with,

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.640
but also the statistics
you find out are crazy.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.810
- Absolutely. I'm so educated on it now.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.410
But the biggest thing is that I love it,

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:30.240
it's a space for women to
be able to communicate,

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.530
tell their stories to
where you don't feel alone.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:35.610
So whether you are going
into, wanting to have a child

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.710
or after childbirth or during childbirth,

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:40.250
there's a whole network of other mommies

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:42.050
and women to be there to encourage you.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:43.200
And I wish I knew about them

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.340
when I was pregnant the first time,

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.173
but I didn't,

00:03:46.173 --> 00:03:48.177
but now that's why I'm
an advocate for them. So.

00:03:48.177 --> 00:03:49.470
(applause)
- Yeah that's amazing.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:50.303
It's amazing.

00:03:50.303 --> 00:03:51.370
So before we go to break,

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:53.210
it's the first day of Black History Month

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:54.450
and you have a special connection

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.020
to the civil rights movement, right?

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:57.003
- Yes, absolutely.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:57.836
- [Kelly] This is awesome, what is it?

00:03:57.836 --> 00:03:59.600
- My grandfather, Reverend Jose Williams,

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.860
the late Reverend Jose
Williams, he worked,

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.726
there's a picture right there
with Dr. Martin Luther king.

00:04:05.726 --> 00:04:06.559
- [Kelly] Wow!

00:04:06.559 --> 00:04:07.570
- He was his right hand, man.

00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:10.760
He used to call my grandfather
the Bull in the China Cabinet

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:13.160
because he was the one
when they went to go march

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.419
and he would get everybody rallied up

00:04:14.419 --> 00:04:17.720
and energized and ready for the march

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:19.170
and in the purpose of the march.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:21.330
And so my grandfather's legacy

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.170
is that he was a civil rights activist

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:25.900
and my family still
runs our family charity.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.510
It's called For Hosea.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:28.436
- That's so cool.

00:04:28.436 --> 00:04:29.269
- [Porsha] Yeah.

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:30.470
- That's an amazing connection. Like,

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.400
especially around this time,
like reminded every year,

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.400
what your family,

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:34.867
those are amazing
footprints to leave behind.

00:04:34.867 --> 00:04:35.700
- Absolutely. and you know,

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.190
Black History Month is a month for us

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:40.650
to really celebrate who we are
and our ancestors before us.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:43.200
So being able to educate the youth,

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.580
and myself even more,

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.490
about so many positive black people

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.510
who have been gone before us

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.610
and their footprints we are now walking in

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:52.317
is such a powerful thing to do.

00:04:52.317 --> 00:04:53.150
(applause)

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:53.983
- And even if you're not black,

00:04:53.983 --> 00:04:55.550
it's an amazing time for everybody

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:56.393
to learn about something
you maybe didn't know.

00:04:56.393 --> 00:04:59.640
- Absolutely, and highlight
the black experience.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.560
So black businesses, e.t.c.

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:03.340
Just let's, everybody we
be black in this mother...

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:05.030
You know? Celebrate!
(chuckling)

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.190
- I just find it really cool.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:08.340
Like I, that's one thing I
love about my kid's school

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.540
is like, there's literally every
walk of life at our school.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:11.800
And I love that from a young,

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.210
cause I grew up like that
when I was really young,

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:15.370
growing up around everything.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.460
And I think that that's really cool

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.680
because then you don't see the differences

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:18.730
and you celebrate everything.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:19.563
It's a magical thing that you.

00:05:19.563 --> 00:05:21.010
- It's what you expose your kids to.

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:23.093
- Absolutely, I agree.
- Absolutely.

